<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY TO AUCTION 5-YR BONDS OF FIVE BLN FORINTS.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY TO AUCTION 5-YR BONDS OF FIVE BLN FORINTS.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction five</p>
<p>billion forint worth of the five-year government bonds of</p>
<p>2002/F series on July 17, the Government Debt Management Agency</p>
<p>(AKK) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest period    July 24, 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity		    June 24, 2002</p>
<p>    Bills on offer			5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price			    94.05 pct</p>
<p>Average price of five-year</p>
<p>     bonds at last auction (June 19)	100.41 pct</p>
<p>    Maximum yield				  16.41 pct</p>
<p>Average yield on five-year</p>
<p>     bonds at last auction (June 19)	 15.41 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 14.00</p>
<p>percent, payable semi-annually starting from December 24, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
